{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784166-gift-of-bone","id":784166,"title":"Gift of Bone","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-11T07:57:54-08:00","id":784166,"title":"Gift of Bone","content":"Below is a Gift list I am making for a game I am running this is the very first draft of some of the Gifts Facets and looking for input on what I have and for ideas on the other two Facets. The general theme of this list is the physical side of Bone hence all the combat facets and strengthening, I will be making a spiritual version later that will deal with the mystical aspect of bones and what they mean. But please take a look and feel free to let me know what you think, this is my first shot at writing Gifts for the new edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Gifts</b><br /> <br /> <b>(Cunning)</b><br /> Unknown<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Spikes (Glory) </b><br /> The Uratha\u2019s bones grow sharp edges and spike the break through the Uratha\u2019s skin greatly adding him in battle.<br /> <b>Activate:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Scene<br /> Upon activating the spikes erupt from his skin causing 1 lethal and granting a weapon bonus equal to the Uratha\u2019s Glory. <br /> <br /> <b>Bones of Stone (Honor)</b><br /> With this Facet the Uratha\u2019s bones become as hard and unbreakable as the earth itself.<br /> <b>Permanent</b><br /> The Uratha\u2019s bones become unbreakable and she gains armor 1/1 <br /> <br /> <b>Blades of Bone (Purity)</b><br /> The Uratha with this facet may never be without a weapon if she so desires for her very bones can produce blades strong as steel.<br /> <b>Activate:</b> 2 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Special<br /> <b>Dice pool:</b> Strength + Weaponry + Purity<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Blade grows inward causing 4L in damage.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> No weapon is created<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Uratha scores successes and draws forth a bone weapon of her desire allocating her success rolled to the weapons damage, size, and durability. The weapon retains these properties for the scene after which time the essence inside the weapon fades and it becomes just a normal peace of bone. If the Uratha has the Bones of Stone Facet the bone weapon is unbreakable for the same duration.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Uratha may invest another point of Essence (or maybe a dote of willpower) to make the weapon retain is bonuses permanently <br /> <br /> <b>(Wisdom)</b><br /> Unknown<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10059-ak_cahalith","name":"AK_Cahalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:39:37-08:00","id":784195,"title":"","content":"I am currently writing up an article re Gift design which may prove useful, but initial comments follow. These will be critical because, well, that's how I approach Gift creation:<br /> <br /> - Gifts don't tend to split a single concept between the physical and spiritual. You're probably better off taking your best ideas for physical and your best ideas for spiritual and putting them all in one Gift, rather than scrabbling for filler Facets to round out the 10 Facets you'd need to cover.<br /> - Bone Spikes is better than Slaughterer in pretty much every way. I would suggest that instead it at least be limited to only adding to damage inflicted in grapples. One-off 1L damage is not a meaningful cost, just flavour, so I wouldn't expect that element to 'buy' it an increased effect for its cost. Possibly it could work if it inflicted 1L on the werewolf every time she uses the damage bonus in a grapple.<br /> - Bones of Stone is not terribly interesting and has an effect that doesn't scale. Additionally, if it's all about strengthening the bones, I'm not sure why it would give armour against attacks rending at the flesh. Instead I'd suggest it add Honor in armour against attacks that are attempting to apply the Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack or Stunned Conditions, although that's just an idea off the top of my head. Additionally, why is this Honor?<br /> - Having Blades of Bone feature a dice pool roll seems a bit pointless; I'd just suggest it provide a weapon with bonus equal to Purity for simplicity. That said, bone is... not really associated with strong, resilient weapons in general, tbh, and given a werewolf already has access to natural weapons I'm not sure why the werewolf expression of the Purity of bones would be to produce bone blades.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T09:55:07-08:00","id":784227,"title":"","content":"As far as Bone Spikes goes I wanted it to be useful all the way around I originally planned for it to be just 1L or 2L so it worked as a small buff that looked really cool. I do agree the lethal is more effect then cost so I\u2019ll do away with it completely.<br /> As for Bones of Stone the flat armor was thinking that yeah you can cut flesh but any time you would hit bone the claw or blades would stop. But I like it being specific to tilts and the like way more actually. As for why Honor because of ideas like, Honor is unshakeable its unbreakable Honor should be steadfast as strong as stone or tougher then steel.<br /> So for Bone Blades and again with the Spikes its one part just really cool effect, one part actually useful. I will admit writing it I was thinking that they have claws and teeth sure this looks bad ass but how often would it be used? So I may do away with it all together and make change Bone Spikes to look slightly more impressive like Wolverine Origen\u2019s style claws or the spikes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10059-ak_cahalith","name":"AK_Cahalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T10:11:29-08:00","id":784230,"title":"","content":"In the vein of Acrozatarim's idea for Bones of Stone, how about if the Wisdom facet offered a Renown bonus on called shots that could lead to broken limb Conditions like Arm or Leg Wrack? As much as I'd like it to be a passive one, these seem to be getting really powerful so perhaps a 1 Essence cost?<br /> <br /> You might take a glimpse at Dar-us the Slow-Killer's abilities for inspiration. Perhaps one of the facets does something similar to Neck Snap, turning overpower damage during grapples to Aggravated?<br /> <br /> Looking at the original Bone gift it looks like Freeze Marrow would be a good one, perhaps offering an alternative Lunacy Condition.<br /> <br /> I recall reading a book that referred to skeletons as cages or temples of bone, where gods and spirits could be held. I'd be for doing something like that but offhand I'm not quite sure how it would work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-11-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T20:39:35-08:00","id":792924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784166-gift-of-bone?p=784230#post784230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall reading a book that referred to skeletons as cages or temples of bone, where gods and spirits could be held. I'd be for doing something like that but offhand I'm not quite sure how it would work.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Witch's Moon ability that does something similar to that. Maybe it might offer ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T03:11:47-08:00","id":793039,"title":"","content":"Here it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u>Cage The Rider (oooo)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence to activate + 1 Essence per scene of entrapment</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Intimidate + Wisdom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Action:</b> Instant</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Many of the spirits that cause the most trouble for Uratha are those that attempt to Ride living creatures. This particularly risky Gift allows the Ithaeur to act as bait to such spirits and then to trap them within herself. Some Ithaeur refer to this Gift as &quot;catching a spirit in my ribcage,&quot; while others liken it to swallowing a spirit for a time or caging a spirit within the mind. Most frequently, this Gift is used either to frighten a spirit into complying with the pack's demands, or as a temporary way to catch a spirit until a formal Rite of Binding or other means of disposal can be prepared.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u>Dramatic Failure:</u> The internal &quot;spirit cage&quot; does not form, but the enticing aura still manifests in a way, drawing the attention of nearby spirits without disguising the werewolf's nature. The Ithaeur is likely to suffer from unwanted spirit attention for the remainder of the scene.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u>Failure:</u> The Gift does not work, and spirits regard the Ithaeur as different in no particular way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u>Success:</u> Until the next moonrise, the Ithaeur exudes a spiritual aura that is particularly enticing to spirits that possess the Living Fetter, Possession or Claim Numina. The werewolf appears to be the ideal host to such a spirit, and the spirit is unlikely to even notice that the Ithaeur is a werewolf at all. Obviously, this Gift is not used lightly; around a nest of spirits with such Numina, it could start a minor war. A spirit that is more than one Rank above the Ithaeur's effective Rank is not affected by this Gift, and most do not notice the lure (though it's possible that one might).<br /> <br /> \u200bWhen a spirit attempts to fetter, claim or possess the Ithaeur via a Numen, the trap activates. The player rolls Intelligence + Occult + Wisdom as a reflexive action to attempt to trap the spirit; the spirit contests the roll by rolling Power. If the roll is a tie or the spirit gets more successes, the Gift effects end, and the spirit breaks free (and may attack or flee, depending on its mental state). If the player gets more successes, though, the spirit is effectively trapped for a scene; the Ithaeur may extend the duration of the imprisonment by spending one Essence per scene. The spirit shares the same space as the Ithaeur, yet cannot break free or manifest itself. The spirit cannot use any Influences or Numina while bound within the Ithaeur. Once per day, at sunrise, the spirit may make a new attempt to break free by rolling Power contested by the Ithaeur's Resolve + Occult. If the spirit breaks free, or is released by the Ithaeur (the Ithaeur may do so at any time as a reflexive action), it wins free of the werewolf's body. If the Ithaeur is in the physical world at this time, the spirit will appear in a state of Twilight. An Ithaeur can have only one spirit bound within her at a time by means of this Gift.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u>Exceptional Success:</u> The trap is particularly cunningly crafted. The player gains two extra dice to the roll made to initially trap the spirit.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I was thinking of adapting this as part of my conversion of Witch's Moon into 2E. Though perhaps this could better fit as the Wisdom Facet for your Gift of Bone? On a semi-related note, this was the 1E Gift I used as the basis for the Cage Tell in this thread of mine.</span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/714377-homebrew-wolf-blooded-tells?p=736699#post736699\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...699#post736699</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T23:54:29-08:00","id":798138,"title":"","content":"some of my ideas, i was half way through writing up a wisdom facet when i remembered that the death gift already had bone gnaw which would essentially be the same thing, will try to come up with more...<br /> <br /> <b>Fractious touch (Cunning facet)</b> it doesn't take brute force to break bones and shatter limbs, all it takes is the right touch in the right place.<br /> Cost: 1 essence<br /> Action: reflexive<br /> the Uratha activates this facet reflexively as part of a touch attack, if the attack is successful the attack deals 1 lethal damage and applies either the Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack tilts until the end of the scene<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bone Spikes (glory facet):</b> how about the lethal damage scales with the damage modifier of the facet so you gain an equipment bonus (glory) weapon but also take (glory) lethal damage. perhaps as an and/or option the damage done when the bone spikes burst out of the characters body can not be healed until the facet has ended and the spikes have contracted? <br /> <br /> <b>(honour facet): </b>I agree with what others have said about bones of stone being a bit underwhelming, though I think simply having it provide (honour) armour rating will still feel a bit meah. I think this facet could do more. how about something like<br /> <br /> Cost: 3 essence<br /> Action: instant<br /> Duration: scene<br /> The Uratha draws strength from the strongest of bonds, the bond of pack, and weaves that strength in to their very bones to keep them whole. The Uratha and her packmates each gain a ballistic armor rating equal the the Uratha's Honour rating and are immune to the effects of the Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack tilts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:50:45-08:00","id":798220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784166-gift-of-bone?p=798138#post798138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some of my ideas, i was half way through writing up a wisdom facet when i remembered that the death gift already had bone gnaw which would essentially be the same thing, will try to come up with more...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fractious Touch seems rather similar to my interpretation of Barbed Arrow for the Gift of Agony. See here... <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion?p=747412#post747412\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...412#post747412</a><br /> <br /> For your Honor Facet, why stop there with ballistic armor? And perhaps Bones of Stone isn't apt at all for it. How about this?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Bones of the Pack</u> [Honor]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Scene<br /> The Uratha draws strength from the strongest of bonds, the bond of pack. And she weaves that strength into her very bones to keep them whole. The Uratha and her packmates each gain Armor rating equal to her Honour Renown, and are immune to the effects of the Arm Wrack and Leg Wrack Tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T08:17:00-08:00","id":798262,"title":"","content":"If you're gonna give flat out, armour rating = Honour to the entire pack then the essence cost needs to be jacked up to five, and/or maybe we put an activation roll in (presence+Medicine+honour?) and it lasts for that many turns instead or the gift becomes far too powerfull. will require significant playtestinjg to get, remember shadow gifts should be rougfhly the equivalent to 3 dot gifts under last edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-08T09:30:59-08:00","id":803805,"title":"","content":"A dice pool of &quot;Presence + Medicine + Honor&quot; works. As does making its duration be a number of turns equal to successes. On the other hand, I got another suggestion, Why not make the immunity to Arm/Leg Wrack be for an Exceptional Success. Either way, here's an updated write-up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Bones of the Pack</u> [Honor]</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence + Medicine + Honor<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Duration: </b>1 Scene<br /> The Uratha draws strength from the strongest of bonds, the bond of pack. And she weaves that strength into her their very bones to keep them whole.<br /> <br /> <u>Dramatic Failure:</u> Not only does the Werewolf fail to activate the Facet, but it rebounds upon her and her packmates as crippling phantom pains. Each member of the pack takes a point of aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <u>Failure</u>: The Facet fails to be invoked.<br /> <br /> <u>Success:</u> The Uratha and her packmates each gain Armor rating equal to her Honour Renown.<br /> <br /> <u>Exceptional Success:</u> In addition to the Armor granted by the Facet, the pack receives an immunity to the Arm and Leg Wrack Tilts for the remainder of the scene. If any of the members is already suffering from either Tilt, it does not affect them until either the end of the scene or the damage that inflicted it is healed.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Also. For the Cunning or Wisdom Facet of the Gift, perhaps a reskin of the Bone Bargain Gift from the Night Horrors supplement of Werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}